{"name":"Mantella Frog","hex":"#ffbc02","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mantella","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any frog of the genus Mantella."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mantella"},{"term":"frog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a class of small tailless amphibians of the order Anura that typically hop.","A member of this class that is not a toad."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt or trap frogs.","To use a pronged plater to transfer (cells) to another plate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mantella","blocks":[{"text":"Mantella are a prominent genus of aposematic frogs in the family Mantellidae, endemic to the island of Madagascar. Members of Mantella are diurnal and terrestrial, with bright aposematic coloration or cryptic markings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/02/Maurantiacamenalamba.jpg/330px-Maurantiacamenalamba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantella","wikidata":"Q1627754"},{"title":"Frog","blocks":[{"text":"A frog is any member of a diverse and largely semiaquatic group of short-bodied, tailless amphibian vertebrates composing the order Anura. Frog species with rough skin texture due to wart-like parotoid glands tend to be called toads, but the distinction between frogs and toads is informal and purely cosmetic, and does not reflect taxonomy or evolutionary history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Red-eyed_Leaf_Frog_%2849661076226%29.jpg/330px-Red-eyed_Leaf_Frog_%2849661076226%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frog","wikidata":"Q53636"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Habitat_at_Vohimana_Experimental_Reserve..jpg/500px-Habitat_at_Vohimana_Experimental_R